 "props": {
  "doc": "Pieces of \"Cold Lips\" (scripts/lips-art-gen.py, scripts/lips-prep.py); this text is props.doc. Puppets (customer, todd) are cut like tip-rig.json's: ONE head (the master's) and a body picture per pose, all in px of the 768x1344 master picture, y down; pivot = the neck. customer.purse[pose] = where the dog goes, in the same px: x, y = the middle of the front edge of the purse's opening (the dog's paws rest on it), w = the purse's outer width just under that edge, inner = [x0, back, x1, front] of the dark inside. todd.badge[pose] = [cx, cy, w, h, angle] of the plain black badge (angle in degrees, 0 = level, clockwise positive; the code writes TODD / MANAGER on it); todd.dryer = box and tip = the nozzle's furthest visible pink pixel in the 'dryer' body (the dryer points at his mouth from the side, so toward +x), waist = the row where that body ends: it is cut off under his belt, 'from the waist up'. props.dog = three pictures of one size and one place (files.neutral, sour, gasp; w, h = their size; anchor = [x, y] in their px: the middle of the paws' span and the bottom edge of the paws, which goes on purse.x, purse.y; paws = [x0, x1] the paws' span at the bottom; fit = how sour and gasp were registered on neutral). props.stripBack = the counter of the plate as a foreground strip (from y0). side = the two profile pieces of the kiss (shot 13), both facing the LEFT of the picture, each one whole-body cut-out in px of its own png (y down), as big as its front master's pictures, so draw it at the scale of the front puppet of the shot: side.customer, side.todd = file, w, h, feet = the y of the feet / floor line, height = the silhouette's, src = the picture it was cut from, head = {face, faceFront, ratio}: the height of the face's skin against the front master's (1 = the same; draw the piece at scale / ratio to match the heads), todd.head also circle [cx, cy, r] through the front outline and rFront, ratioCircle against the master's disc; customer.seat = [x, y] the rearmost point of her coat, where the lips land; customer.purse = {x, y, w, inner} like customer.purse[pose] (the dog goes there: props.dog.anchor on x, y); todd.lips = [x, y] the front tip of his pucker; side.kneel = what that makes at the kneeling shot's scales (src/lips-layout.ts KNEEL, read when this was made), in frame px: herFeet, herSeatUp, hisLipsUp = the heights above the feet of her seat and of his lips, floorDelta = his floor minus hers with his lips on her seat, tEOneFloor = the Todd scale that puts them on one floor. scenes.cafeBack = the plate lips-bg-cafeBack.jpg: frame and door = the doorway's outer frame and its empty opening [x0, y0, x1, y1] (the glass door is drawn in code, as in src/tip-scenes.tsx CafeDoor), window, floor = where the floor meets the wall panelling, counterTop = the counter's far edge (the foreground strip starts there), lip = its front edge.",
